I have a complete picture. Here are my findings.

## 1. The business-day rule (core logic)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BusinessDay.java`**

The single source of the rule. A stateless final utility class with one static method `onOrAfter(LocalDate)`:

```java
public static LocalDate onOrAfter(LocalDate date) {
    DayOfWeek day = date.getDayOfWeek();
    if (day == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY) {
        return date.plusDays(2);
    }
    if (day == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY) {
        return date.plusDays(1);
    }
    return date;
}
```

Rolls a Saturday forward to Monday and a Sunday forward to Monday; returns weekdays unchanged. Note: **only weekends are handled — there is no public-holiday handling** despite what test comments imply (see below).

## 2. Where the registration date is actually computed/adjusted

The authoritative computation is in the JPA entity lifecycle callback:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** (lines 423–429), method `resolveRegistrationDate()`, annotated `@PrePersist`:

```java
@PrePersist
private void resolveRegistrationDate() {
    if (this.registrationDate == null) {
        this.registrationDate = LocalDate.now();
    }
    this.registrationDate = BusinessDay.onOrAfter(this.registrationDate);
}
```

This defaults a missing date to today, then applies the business-day roll before persisting. Values derived from it (e.g. `getMembershipNumber()` at line 295) use the adjusted date.

`BusinessDay.onOrAfter` is also called in two other places to stay consistent with the stored date:
- **`.../rest/validation/DailyOwnerLimitValidator.java`** (lines 52–55) — rolls the supplied/current date before counting owners for the daily-limit check.
- **`.../rest/signup/BulkSignupWarningEvaluator.java`** (line 46) — rolls today's date before the bulk-signup threshold check.

Related (but NOT business-day) registration-date code:
- **`.../rest/validation/RegistrationDateValidator.java`** — only rejects future dates (`isAfter(LocalDate.now())`); does no weekend/holiday adjustment.
- Controller wiring in **`.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (lines 196–197) invokes both validators on create.

## 3. Existing tests for the business-day logic

There is **no dedicated unit test for `BusinessDay`**. The only coverage is one black-box acceptance test:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`**

```java
@Test
void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
    DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(
            fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(structuredOwner())).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
    assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
}
```

What it asserts: after creating an owner with no supplied date and fetching it back, the returned `registrationDate` is never a Saturday or Sunday.

Important discrepancy: the file's header comment (lines 9–11) claims "the default registration date rolls past public holidays as well as weekends" and describes this as an invariant that "subsumes" holiday handling. But the actual `BusinessDay` code handles weekends only — there is no holiday logic anywhere in the codebase. The test only verifies the weekend invariant. Helper methods `createOwnerOk`, `fetchOwner`, `structuredOwner` live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`.

## 4. How dates/holidays are represented

- **Dates:** `java.time.LocalDate` throughout. `Owner.registrationDate` is a `LocalDate` field (Owner.java line 69, getter/setter 184–189). Persisted via JPA; queried by `countByRegistrationDate` in the JPA/JDBC/Spring-Data repositories (e.g. JDBC column `registration_date` in `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` line 267).
- **Business day:** derived on the fly from `DayOfWeek` inside `BusinessDay.onOrAfter`; not stored or modeled as a type.
- **Holidays:** **not represented at all.** There is no holiday calendar, no holiday list, no config/resource for holidays, and no `Holiday` type anywhere in the project. Only weekends are recognized. Any holiday-adjustment requirement is currently unimplemented (the acceptance-test comment referring to holidays is aspirational and not backed by code).

